      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VICI BLOOM (6) has looked good in winning both of her starts at this circuit and distance since a lengthy spell. Draws wider this time but should be at her peak third-up and winning form is hard to knock. MAORIS MAC (9) was very consistent with a string of placings at the end of her last campaign, the last two coming at Group 1 level behind might mare Keayang Zahara. Hasn't raced for 10 months and is yet to win when fresh but has placed in three of five attempts and she has been readied with two trials. SAM NIEN (5) powered back to form at the right time last week, coming from this barrier for an upset win in the Vicbred final at this circuit and distance. Could go on with it. RUBYS DREAM (7) draws wider than in last week's win but strikes at 50 per cent when third-up so could be further improved. QUIRKY CHARACTER (8) could be close to a return to winning form having placed in his last two outings, the latest from this barrier.",
